      "side": 1,
      "message": "I updated things to support json primitive types so str, int, float, null should all work now in addition to zuul regexes. The reason I didn\u0027t add list and dict as well is that a zuul regex is a dict and I\u0027m not sure there is a good way to distinguish a zuul regex dict from an arbitrary dict to match. I figured if we aren\u0027t doing dicts then not doing lists avoids confusion in behavior.\n\nBut if we want to do lists and arbitrary dicts and can think of a good way to represent that within the zuul config without confusing users we can update this change to do that.",
      "parentUuid": "a850137b_77caf7cf",
      "revId": "4f6b63f2969919a04d58b6e874579dbfef323d52",
